cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Scaffale: local indexing, OCR and semantic search of a personal research archive with a local language model"
version: "1.0"
abstract: "Scaffale takes a disordered research folder (PDFs, Word files, notes, spreadsheets, old databases, scans, folders of photographed pages) and turns it into a searchable archive with exact, thesaurus-based and semantic search, a link to the right page of every passage, questions to the documents answered with numbered sources, groups, themes and summaries, and OCR in nine languages. PDFs and scans are converted to Markdown with three independent readings: every line with numbers or dates is read by two OCR readers and, where they disagree, a third reader (PaddleOCR) acts as arbiter; unconfirmed lines are flagged for checking on the original. Everything runs on the local computer: the language models (bge-m3, qwen3:8b, glm-ocr) are installed locally through Ollama and no document is uploaded. Developed for the author's historical research archive (about 15,000 documents), it made possible the corpus-wide study of the sources on the Madonna Nicopeia, and it is presented in the author's doctoral work as a first case study of a local language model applied to the semantic analysis of archives, including historical ones."
authors:
  - family-names: Sbarbaro
    given-names: Massimo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8965-9013"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
date-released: "2026-11-08"
repository-code: "https://github.com/massimosbarbaro/scaffale"
keywords:
